      "title": "A policy loan uses the policy as security",
      "narration": "Marcus wants money for a family expense while keeping his life policy. If his contract has sufficient available loan value and he has the required rights, he can request a policy loan. The insurer advances money with the policy as security. This is different from an unrelated bank loan and different from withdrawing part of the policy's value. Policy debt carries interest and affects the amount ultimately available on surrender or death. The face amount alone does not establish how much Marcus can borrow. Read the current loan value, existing debt, applicable rate and conditions before explaining the available amount.",
