      "title": "Using a loan for education does not change its mechanics",
      "narration": "Marcus considers borrowing five thousand dollars against available policy value to help pay tuition. Paying a college bill does not transform that advance into a scholarship, federal student loan or tax-favored education account. It remains a policy loan with its own interest, effect on benefits and risk if debt grows. Compare the family's remaining protection needs and other funding resources before committing. The word educational describes the intended use in this example, not a universal separate policy rider. A producer should explain the real terms and avoid promising unlimited or cost-free access to the policy's death benefit.",
